{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-143581",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We're given $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $Y$ when $0\\le y\\le 3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{3}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{3}(\\frac{2}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\cdot \\frac{2y}{9}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(9-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5X-Y] & =5\\,\\text{E}[X]+(-1)\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =5(\\frac{3}{5})+(-1)(2) \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
